> I incorrectly stated problems with RME Multiface, it works with 1.0.12.
> Echo Indigo IO does not. And there's a new file in .12 - loader_dsp.fw.
> I suppose, echo firmware loading was changed.

loader_dsp.fw is an unused file, and I already got rid of it from ALSA
HG tree.  So, the rest isn't changed.

I guess the problem of firmware loading was fixed by 1.0.13rc1
package.  There was a problem in configure script that it resets the
kernel CONFIG_FW_LOADER* acciedentally, which results in the driver
without firmware support.

> As for multiface, patch did not help. I stiil have to replug cardbus
> if I power-cycle multiface box. 

Hm, could you check whether a kernel message like "Hammerfall-DSP:
loading firmware" appears?  This should be called when a PCM device is
opened, or any new PCM action is done.

> hdsploader still gives:
> Upload firmware for card hw:0
> Hwdep ioctl error on card hw:0 : Device or resource busy.

This isn't changed because it doesn't make sense if the auto-reloading
works.  As mentioned, the image is saved in the driver.


